    <section>
      <div class="narrow prose">
        <p class="kicker">The polls are the admissions test</p>
        <h2>A state that wants religious law does not get to export the electorate.</h2>
        <p>The pause is not a guess about every person in a passport queue. It is a rule about the polity. If a majority of adults in the sending state say they want religious law to govern, the receiving state is entitled to stop issuing the visa. Private dissenters inside that state are not a reason to import the majority’s law.</p>
<p>Use the Pew questions without mixing them. In 2013, asked whether sharia should be the official law, 99 percent in Afghanistan and 84 percent in Pakistan said yes. On January 28, 2025, Pew reported that adults in Bangladesh, Indonesia, and Malaysia more often say the Quran should outweigh the will of the people when the two conflict, including 77 percent in Bangladesh. Different years. Different sentences. Same direction: scripture over the electorate.</p>
<p>Sweden is the control group for a stupid version of this pause. Brå 2025:7 finds under-representation, or no overrepresentation, among migrants from high-income countries and among people admitted for work or study, and higher rates from low-income and conflict origins. A serious pause aims at the second group, not at a Japanese engineer or a Korean graduate student. Germany’s pattern is the same shape. Japanese and Chinese nationals are not the non-German overrepresentation.</p>
<p>Rotherham is what it looks like when institutions refuse the specific noun. The Jay inquiry in 2014 found at least 1,400 children exploited from 1997 to 2013, and found that authorities looked away partly for fear of racism accusations. A statute that will not name origin will not protect the next town either.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="narrow prose">
        <p class="kicker">04</p>
        <h2>What the demand is not.</h2>
        <p>It is not a call to harm a person, citizen or not. It is not a slur. It is not “anyone Muslim, out,” and anyone who shortens it to that is writing a different document.</p>
<p>It is not a claim that every non-German suspect in the BKA tables is Muslim. Nationality is not a religion census, dual nationals are counted as German, and Albania’s presence on the boat list is the standing correction. The demand does not need a false census. It needs the origin pattern and the law those origins say they want.</p>
<p>It is not an announcement that the United States has some secret annual removal quota this page refuses to print. We are not inventing a border number. Removal of people with no right to remain is ordinary Immigration and Nationality Act practice. The missing American number is not an argument for leaving failed claimants in place.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <div class="narrow prose">
        <h2>Citizens are not the cargo. Welfare is not a settlement program.</h2>
        <p>Chain migration is how a pause gets undone. One admission becomes a household, then a street, then a voting bloc organized around the law of the sending state. End the chain. The person who is already a citizen stays a citizen. The person who is not does not acquire cousins as a right.</p>
<p>Welfare is for citizens. A non-citizen with no right to remain is not a client the public has adopted. Housing, asylum support, and municipal services are not a back door into permanent settlement when the claim has failed or the visa has lapsed.</p>
<p>The record sits on demandremigration.com: Germany’s 35.5 percent suspect share against a 14.9 percent population share, Sweden’s gap after controls, the Channel boats, the two Pew questions kept separate. nozabiha.com and nozabihahalal.com refuse the religious food code. islamophobe.me refuses the legal system that travels with it. This page is the removal.</p>
        <p><a href="https://demandremigration.com/">Continue to demandremigration.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sand">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="kicker">The line in the sand</p>
        <h2>Remigration of Muslim immigrants who have no permanent right to remain, and a pause on new admission from states that want religious law, is the compatible policy. A continued import is not.</h2>
        <div class="prose"><p>Western law is one law, made by the living electorate, applied without a religious test and without a religious exemption that swallows the rule. A sending society that rejects that arrangement does not have a claim on the visa window.</p>
<p>Enforcement is removal under statute, after process, of people the law already does not entitle to stay — plus a legislative pause where the polls are this clear. It is not a riot, and it is not a hereditary exile of citizens.</p>
<p>We are not going to become compatible with the alternative. The alternative is the suspect table, the boat, the child-exploitation inquiry that was not allowed to name what it saw, and a food code and a legal code that do not mean to sit politely beside civil law.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="act">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>What the statute looks like.</h2>
        <div class="action-grid"><article class="action">
        <h3>Remove people with no right to remain</h3>
        <p>Illegal entry, visa overstay, and failed asylum are not a second citizenship. Removal is already the ordinary rule. Enforce it. Do not invent a new one for people the statute already covers.</p>
      </article>
<article class="action">
        <h3>Sentence, then departure</h3>
        <p>A non-citizen convicted of a removable crime serves the sentence and leaves. Prison is not an integration program and it is not a path to settlement.</p>
      </article>
<article class="action">
        <h3>Pause the sending states</h3>
        <p>Stop new visas and resettlement from states where majorities tell pollsters they want religious law over civil law. That is an admissions rule about the polity people are leaving, not a raid on a citizen’s house.</p>
      </article>
<article class="action">
        <h3>Stop rebuilding the origin</h3>
        <p>Chain migration restocks the sending society inside the receiving one. End it. Welfare is for citizens. A lawful permanent resident who has not committed a removable offense, and has not naturalized by fraud, is not the cargo.</p>
      </article></div>
        <div class="panel" style="margin-top:2.5rem;background:transparent">
          <p class="closer">Remigration does not riot. It removes.</p>
          <p>No right to remain means leave. Citizens are not the cargo.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
